{"p":"/physics/sleep-system","t":"Sleep system","d":"Explore how the sleep system automatically prevents unnecessary simulation of non-moving parts.","h":"<p>Each <a href=\"#/docs/physics/assemblies\">assembly</a> in the Roblox Engine corresponds to a single <strong>rigid body</strong>. The position and velocity of each rigid body describe where it's located and how fast it's moving, and one of the primary engine tasks is to update the positions and velocities of each assembly.</p>\n<p>Assemblies can be connected together with <a href=\"#/docs/physics/mechanical-constraints\">mechanical constraints</a> and <a href=\"#/docs/physics/mover-constraints\">mover constraints</a> to form mechanisms such as cars or airplanes. As the number of assemblies and constraints in a mechanism increases, the time required to simulate the mechanism also increases. Fortunately, this increase is offset when the <strong>sleep system</strong> determines that the engine can skip simulation of non‑moving assemblies.</p>\n<h2>Sleep states</h2>\n<p>Each assembly can be in one of three states: <a href=\"#awake\">awake</a>, <a href=\"#sleeping\">sleeping</a>, or <a href=\"#sleep-checking\">sleep‑checking</a>.</p>\n<h3>Awake</h3>\n<p>An <strong>awake</strong> assembly is moving or accelerating, and is therefore simulated. Assemblies enter this state from situations outlined in <a href=\"#sleeping\">sleeping</a> and <a href=\"#sleep-checking\">sleep‑checking</a>, as well as <a href=\"#additional-wake-situations\">additional wake situations</a>.</p>\n<h3>Sleeping</h3>\n<p>A <strong>sleeping</strong> assembly is neither moving nor accelerating, and is therefore not simulated.</p>\n<p>An assembly is determined to be non-moving by checking its <strong>linear velocity</strong> and <strong>rotational velocity</strong>. If its linear velocity is less than the <a href=\"#threshold-reference\">Linear&nbsp;Velocity</a> threshold and its rotational velocity is less than the <a href=\"#threshold-reference\">Rotational&nbsp;Velocity</a> threshold, the assembly is considered to be non-moving.</p>\n<p>In some cases, simply checking for non-movement would cause an assembly to incorrectly enter the sleeping state. For example, if a ball is thrown straight up, its velocity approaches zero as it reaches its maximum height, making it a candidate to sleep and never fall back down. To handle such cases, the engine considers an assembly to be accelerating if its <strong>linear acceleration</strong> or <strong>rotational acceleration</strong> are greater than the <a href=\"#threshold-reference\">Linear&nbsp;Acceleration</a> and <a href=\"#threshold-reference\">Rotational&nbsp;Acceleration</a> thresholds, respectively, and will prevent the assembly from falling asleep.</p>\n<div class=\"callout c-info\">\n<p>If an assembly falls asleep when you expect it to remain awake, it's commonly because the assembly is moving too slowly. In addition to automatic checks outlined in <a href=\"#sleep-checking\">sleep‑checking</a> and <a href=\"#sleeping\">sleeping</a>, you can forcibly wake up an assembly through the conditions outlined in <a href=\"#additional-wake-situations\">additional wake situations</a>.</p>\n</div>\n<h3>Sleep-checking</h3>\n<p>A non-moving assembly that shares a constraint with at least one <a href=\"#awake\">awake</a> neighboring assembly is put into the <strong>sleep-checking</strong> state and is not simulated. On each worldstep, a sleep-checking assembly checks whether:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Its <strong>linear acceleration</strong> is greater than the <a href=\"#threshold-reference\">Wake&nbsp;Linear&nbsp;Acceleration</a> threshold.</li>\n<li>Its <strong>rotational acceleration</strong> is greater than the <a href=\"#threshold-reference\">Wake&nbsp;Rotational&nbsp;Acceleration</a> threshold.</li>\n<li>A neighboring assembly's <strong>linear velocity</strong> is greater than the <a href=\"#threshold-reference\">Neighbor&nbsp;Linear&nbsp;Velocity</a> threshold.</li>\n<li>A neighboring assembly's <strong>rotational velocity</strong> is greater than the <a href=\"#threshold-reference\">Neighbor&nbsp;Rotational&nbsp;Velocity</a> threshold.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>If any of these conditions is true, or under any of the <a href=\"#additional-wake-situations\">additional wake situations</a>, the sleep-checking assembly enters the <a href=\"#awake\">awake</a> state.</p>\n<h2>Threshold reference</h2>\n<p>The following table provides the various velocity and acceleration thresholds used to determine if an assembly is moving or accelerating.</p>\n<table>\n<thead>\n    <tr>\n        <th>Threshold</th>\n        <th>Value</th>\n        <th>State change</th>\n    </tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n    <tr>\n        <td>Linear Velocity</td>\n        <td>0.33 studs/s</td>\n        <td>[awake](#awake) &rang; [sleeping](#sleeping)</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n        <td>Rotational Velocity</td>\n        <td>0.42 studs/s</td>\n        <td>[awake](#awake) &rang; [sleeping](#sleeping)</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n        <td>Linear Acceleration</td>\n        <td>0.24 studs/s&sup2;</td>\n        <td>[awake](#awake) &rang; [sleeping](#sleeping)</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n        <td>Rotational Acceleration</td>\n        <td>0.24 studs/s&sup2;</td>\n        <td>[awake](#awake) &rang; [sleeping](#sleeping)</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n        <td>Neighbor Linear Velocity</td>\n        <td>0.48 studs/s</td>\n        <td>[sleep-checking](#sleep-checking) &rang; [awake](#awake)</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n        <td>Neighbor Rotational Velocity</td>\n        <td>0.59 studs/s</td>\n        <td>[sleep-checking](#sleep-checking) &rang; [awake](#awake)</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n        <td>Wake Linear Acceleration</td>\n        <td>16.9 studs/s&sup2;</td>\n        <td>[awake](#awake) &rang; [sleeping](#sleeping)</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n        <td>Wake Rotational Acceleration</td>\n        <td>16.9 studs/s&sup2;</td>\n        <td>[awake](#awake) &rang; [sleeping](#sleeping)</td>\n    </tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n\n<p>Rotational velocity and acceleration thresholds reflect the velocity and acceleration of a point located on the assembly bounding sphere (a sphere that contains all of the parts in an assembly) that moves rigidly with the assembly.</p>\n<div class=\"callout c-info\">\n<p>For a given angular velocity, the rotational velocity of an assembly is proportional to the assembly bounding sphere radius. This means that larger assemblies can rotate at a lower angular velocity without falling asleep.</p>\n</div>\n<h2>Actuated joints</h2>\n<p>Sometimes developers want to move parts very slowly using an <strong>actuated joint</strong>, a constraint that applies force or motion to drive connected parts, such as a <a class=\"ref\" href=\"#/class/HingeConstraint\"><code>HingeConstraint</code></a> using a <a class=\"ref\" href=\"#/enum/ActuatorType/ActuatorType.Motor\"><code>Motor</code></a>. To support these scenarios, assemblies connected to actuated joints use a stricter sleep velocity threshold. This delays when those assemblies fall asleep, allowing slow, controlled motion without the physics system prematurely putting them to sleep.</p>\n<p>The following are considered actuated joints:</p>\n<table>\n    <thead>\n        <tr>\n            <th>Constraint</th>\n            <th>Configuration</th>\n            <th>Required nonzero properties</th>\n        </tr>\n    </thead>\n    <tbody>\n        <tr>\n            <td><a class=\"ref\" href=\"#/class/AlignOrientation\"><code>AlignOrientation</code></a></td>\n            <td><a class=\"ref\" href=\"#/class/AlignOrientation/AlignOrientation.RigidityEnabled\"><code>RigidityEnabled</code></a> = `false`</td>\n            <td>\n                <ul>\n                    <li><a class=\"ref\" href=\"#/class/AlignOrientation/AlignOrientation.MaxAngularVelocity\"><code>MaxAngularVelocity</code></a></li>\n                    <li><a class=\"ref\" href=\"#/class/AlignOrientation/AlignOrientation.MaxTorque\"><code>MaxTorque</code></a></li>\n                    <li><a class=\"ref\" href=\"#/class/AlignOrientation/AlignOrientation.Responsiveness\"><code>Responsiveness</code></a></li>\n                </ul>\n            </td>\n        </tr>\n        <tr>\n            <td><a class=\"ref\" href=\"#/class/AlignPosition\"><code>AlignPosition</code></a></td>\n            <td><a class=\"ref\" href=\"#/class/AlignPosition/AlignPosition.RigidityEnabled\"><code>RigidityEnabled</code></a> = `false`</td>\n            <td>\n                <ul>\n                    <li><a class=\"ref\" href=\"#/class/AlignPosition/AlignPosition.MaxVelocity\"><code>MaxVelocity</code></a></li>\n                    <li><a class=\"ref\" href=\"#/class/AlignPosition/AlignPosition.Responsiveness\"><code>Responsiveness</code></a></li>\n                </ul>\n            </td>\n        </tr>\n        <tr>\n            <td><a class=\"ref\" href=\"#/class/AngularVelocity\"><code>AngularVelocity</code></a></td>\n            <td>—</td>\n            <td>\n                <ul>\n                    <li><a class=\"ref\" href=\"#/class/AngularVelocity/AngularVelocity.AngularVelocity\"><code>AngularVelocity</code></a></li>\n                    <li><a class=\"ref\" href=\"#/class/AngularVelocity/AngularVelocity.MaxTorque\"><code>MaxTorque</code></a></li>\n                </ul>\n            </td>\n        </tr>\n        <tr>\n            <td><a class=\"ref\" href=\"#/class/AnimationConstraint\"><code>AnimationConstraint</code></a></td>\n            <td><a class=\"ref\" href=\"#/class/AnimationConstraint/AnimationConstraint.IsKinematic\"><code>IsKinematic</code></a> = `false`</td>\n            <td>\n                <ul>\n                    <li><a class=\"ref\" href=\"#/class/AnimationConstraint/AnimationConstraint.MaxForce\"><code>MaxForce</code></a></li>\n                    <li><a class=\"ref\" href=\"#/class/AnimationConstraint/AnimationConstraint.MaxTorque\"><code>MaxTorque</code></a></li>\n                </ul>\n            </td>\n        </tr>\n        <tr>\n            <td rowspan=\"2\"><a class=\"ref\" href=\"#/class/CylindricalConstraint\"><code>CylindricalConstraint</code></a></td>\n            <td><a class=\"ref\" href=\"#/class/CylindricalConstraint/CylindricalConstraint.ActuatorType\"><code>ActuatorType</code></a> = <a class=\"ref\" href=\"#/enum/ActuatorType/ActuatorType.Motor\"><code>Motor</code></a></td>\n            <td>\n                <ul>\n                    <li><a class=\"ref\" href=\"#/class/CylindricalConstraint/CylindricalConstraint.Velocity\"><code>Velocity</code></a></li>\n                    <li><a class=\"ref\" href=\"#/class/CylindricalConstraint/CylindricalConstraint.MotorMaxAcceleration\"><code>MotorMaxAcceleration</code></a></li>\n                    <li><a class=\"ref\" href=\"#/class/CylindricalConstraint/CylindricalConstraint.MotorMaxForce\"><code>MotorMaxForce</code></a></li>\n                </ul>\n            </td>\n        </tr>\n        <tr>\n            <td><a class=\"ref\" href=\"#/class/CylindricalConstraint/CylindricalConstraint.ActuatorType\"><code>ActuatorType</code></a> = <a class=\"ref\" href=\"#/enum/ActuatorType/ActuatorType.Servo\"><code>Servo</code></a></td>\n            <td>\n                <ul>\n                    <li><a class=\"ref\" href=\"#/class/CylindricalConstraint/CylindricalConstraint.Speed\"><code>Speed</code></a></li>\n                    <li><a class=\"ref\" href=\"#/class/CylindricalConstraint/CylindricalConstraint.ServoMaxForce\"><code>ServoMaxForce</code></a></li>\n                    <li><a class=\"ref\" href=\"#/class/CylindricalConstraint/CylindricalConstraint.Responsiveness\"><code>Responsiveness</code></a></li>\n                </ul>\n            </td>\n        </tr>\n        <tr>\n            <td rowspan=\"2\"><a class=\"ref\" href=\"#/class/CylindricalConstraint\"><code>CylindricalConstraint</code></a></td>\n            <td><a class=\"ref\" href=\"#/class/CylindricalConstraint/CylindricalConstraint.AngularActuatorType\"><code>AngularActuatorType</code></a> = <a class=\"ref\" href=\"#/enum/ActuatorType/ActuatorType.Motor\"><code>Motor</code></a></td>\n            <td>\n                <ul>\n                    <li><a class=\"ref\" href=\"#/class/CylindricalConstraint/CylindricalConstraint.AngularVelocity\"><code>AngularVelocity</code></a></li>\n                    <li><a class=\"ref\" href=\"#/class/CylindricalConstraint/CylindricalConstraint.MotorMaxAngularAcceleration\"><code>MotorMaxAngularAcceleration</code></a></li>\n                    <li><a class=\"ref\" href=\"#/class/CylindricalConstraint/CylindricalConstraint.MotorMaxTorque\"><code>MotorMaxTorque</code></a></li>\n                </ul>\n            </td>\n        </tr>\n        <tr>\n            <td><a class=\"ref\" href=\"#/class/CylindricalConstraint/CylindricalConstraint.AngularActuatorType\"><code>AngularActuatorType</code></a> = <a class=\"ref\" href=\"#/enum/ActuatorType/ActuatorType.Servo\"><code>Servo</code></a></td>\n            <td>\n                <ul>\n                    <li><a class=\"ref\" href=\"#/class/CylindricalConstraint/CylindricalConstraint.AngularSpeed\"><code>AngularSpeed</code></a></li>\n                    <li><a class=\"ref\" href=\"#/class/CylindricalConstraint/CylindricalConstraint.ServoMaxTorque\"><code>ServoMaxTorque</code></a></li>\n                    <li><a class=\"ref\" href=\"#/class/CylindricalConstraint/CylindricalConstraint.Responsiveness\"><code>Responsiveness</code></a></li>\n                </ul>\n            </td>\n        </tr>\n        <tr>\n            <td rowspan=\"2\"><a class=\"ref\" href=\"#/class/HingeConstraint\"><code>HingeConstraint</code></a></td>\n            <td><a class=\"ref\" href=\"#/class/HingeConstraint/HingeConstraint.ActuatorType\"><code>ActuatorType</code></a> = <a class=\"ref\" href=\"#/enum/ActuatorType/ActuatorType.Motor\"><code>Motor</code></a></td>\n            <td>\n                <ul>\n                    <li><a class=\"ref\" href=\"#/class/HingeConstraint/HingeConstraint.AngularVelocity\"><code>AngularVelocity</code></a></li>\n                    <li><a class=\"ref\" href=\"#/class/HingeConstraint/HingeConstraint.MotorMaxAcceleration\"><code>MotorMaxAcceleration</code></a></li>\n                    <li><a class=\"ref\" href=\"#/class/HingeConstraint/HingeConstraint.MotorMaxTorque\"><code>MotorMaxTorque</code></a></li>\n                </ul>\n            </td>\n        </tr>\n        <tr>\n            <td><a class=\"ref\" href=\"#/class/HingeConstraint/HingeConstraint.ActuatorType\"><code>ActuatorType</code></a> = <a class=\"ref\" href=\"#/enum/ActuatorType/ActuatorType.Servo\"><code>Servo</code></a></td>\n            <td>\n                <ul>\n                    <li><a class=\"ref\" href=\"#/class/HingeConstraint/HingeConstraint.AngularSpeed\"><code>AngularSpeed</code></a></li>\n                    <li><a class=\"ref\" href=\"#/class/HingeConstraint/HingeConstraint.ServoMaxTorque\"><code>ServoMaxTorque</code></a></li>\n                    <li><a class=\"ref\" href=\"#/class/HingeConstraint/HingeConstraint.Responsiveness\"><code>Responsiveness</code></a></li>\n                </ul>\n            </td>\n        </tr>\n        <tr>\n            <td rowspan=\"3\"><a class=\"ref\" href=\"#/class/LinearVelocity\"><code>LinearVelocity</code></a></td>\n            <td><a class=\"ref\" href=\"#/class/LinearVelocity/LinearVelocity.VelocityConstraintMode\"><code>VelocityConstraintMode</code></a> = <a class=\"ref\" href=\"#/enum/VelocityConstraintMode/VelocityConstraintMode.Line\"><code>Line</code></a></td>\n            <td>\n                <ul>\n                    <li><a class=\"ref\" href=\"#/class/LinearVelocity/LinearVelocity.LineVelocity\"><code>LineVelocity</code></a></li>\n                    <li>If <a class=\"ref\" href=\"#/class/LinearVelocity/LinearVelocity.ForceLimitsEnabled\"><code>ForceLimitsEnabled</code></a>, also <a class=\"ref\" href=\"#/class/LinearVelocity/LinearVelocity.MaxForce\"><code>MaxForce</code></a></li>\n                </ul>\n            </td>\n        </tr>\n        <tr>\n            <td><a class=\"ref\" href=\"#/class/LinearVelocity/LinearVelocity.VelocityConstraintMode\"><code>VelocityConstraintMode</code></a> = <a class=\"ref\" href=\"#/enum/VelocityConstraintMode/VelocityConstraintMode.Plane\"><code>Plane</code></a></td>\n            <td>\n                <ul>\n                    <li><a class=\"ref\" href=\"#/class/LinearVelocity/LinearVelocity.PlaneVelocity\"><code>PlaneVelocity</code></a></li>\n                    <li>\n                        <span>If <a class=\"ref\" href=\"#/class/LinearVelocity/LinearVelocity.ForceLimitsEnabled\"><code>ForceLimitsEnabled</code></a>:</span>\n                        <ul>\n                            <li><a class=\"ref\" href=\"#/enum/ForceLimitMode/ForceLimitMode.Magnitude\"><code>Magnitude</code></a>: <a class=\"ref\" href=\"#/class/LinearVelocity/LinearVelocity.MaxForce\"><code>MaxForce</code></a></li>\n                            <li><a class=\"ref\" href=\"#/enum/ForceLimitMode/ForceLimitMode.PerAxis\"><code>PerAxis</code></a>: <a class=\"ref\" href=\"#/class/LinearVelocity/LinearVelocity.MaxPlanarAxesForce\"><code>MaxPlanarAxesForce</code></a></li>\n                        </ul>\n                    </li>\n                </ul>\n            </td>\n        </tr>\n        <tr>\n            <td><a class=\"ref\" href=\"#/class/LinearVelocity/LinearVelocity.VelocityConstraintMode\"><code>VelocityConstraintMode</code></a> = <a class=\"ref\" href=\"#/enum/VelocityConstraintMode/VelocityConstraintMode.Vector\"><code>Vector</code></a></td>\n            <td>\n                <ul>\n                    <li><a class=\"ref\" href=\"#/class/LinearVelocity/LinearVelocity.VectorVelocity\"><code>VectorVelocity</code></a></li>\n                    <li>\n                        <span>If <a class=\"ref\" href=\"#/class/LinearVelocity/LinearVelocity.ForceLimitsEnabled\"><code>ForceLimitsEnabled</code></a>:</span>\n                        <ul>\n                            <li><a class=\"ref\" href=\"#/enum/ForceLimitMode/ForceLimitMode.Magnitude\"><code>Magnitude</code></a>: <a class=\"ref\" href=\"#/class/LinearVelocity/LinearVelocity.MaxForce\"><code>MaxForce</code></a></li>\n                            <li><a class=\"ref\" href=\"#/enum/ForceLimitMode/ForceLimitMode.PerAxis\"><code>PerAxis</code></a>: <a class=\"ref\" href=\"#/class/LinearVelocity/LinearVelocity.MaxAxesForce\"><code>MaxAxesForce</code></a></li>\n                        </ul>\n                    </li>\n                </ul>\n            </td>\n        </tr>\n        <tr>\n            <td rowspan=\"2\"><a class=\"ref\" href=\"#/class/PrismaticConstraint\"><code>PrismaticConstraint</code></a></td>\n            <td><a class=\"ref\" href=\"#/class/PrismaticConstraint/PrismaticConstraint.ActuatorType\"><code>ActuatorType</code></a> = <a class=\"ref\" href=\"#/enum/ActuatorType/ActuatorType.Motor\"><code>Motor</code></a></td>\n            <td>\n                <ul>\n                    <li><a class=\"ref\" href=\"#/class/PrismaticConstraint/PrismaticConstraint.Velocity\"><code>Velocity</code></a></li>\n                    <li><a class=\"ref\" href=\"#/class/PrismaticConstraint/PrismaticConstraint.MotorMaxAcceleration\"><code>MotorMaxAcceleration</code></a></li>\n                    <li><a class=\"ref\" href=\"#/class/PrismaticConstraint/PrismaticConstraint.MotorMaxForce\"><code>MotorMaxForce</code></a></li>\n                </ul>\n            </td>\n        </tr>\n        <tr>\n            <td><a class=\"ref\" href=\"#/class/PrismaticConstraint/PrismaticConstraint.ActuatorType\"><code>ActuatorType</code></a> = <a class=\"ref\" href=\"#/enum/ActuatorType/ActuatorType.Servo\"><code>Servo</code></a></td>\n            <td>\n                <ul>\n                    <li><a class=\"ref\" href=\"#/class/PrismaticConstraint/PrismaticConstraint.Speed\"><code>Speed</code></a></li>\n                    <li><a class=\"ref\" href=\"#/class/PrismaticConstraint/PrismaticConstraint.ServoMaxForce\"><code>ServoMaxForce</code></a></li>\n                    <li><a class=\"ref\" href=\"#/class/PrismaticConstraint/PrismaticConstraint.Responsiveness\"><code>Responsiveness</code></a></li>\n                </ul>\n            </td>\n        </tr>\n        <tr>\n            <td><a class=\"ref\" href=\"#/class/RopeConstraint\"><code>RopeConstraint</code></a></td>\n            <td><a class=\"ref\" href=\"#/class/RopeConstraint/RopeConstraint.WinchEnabled\"><code>WinchEnabled</code></a> = `true`</td>\n            <td>\n                <ul>\n                    <li><a class=\"ref\" href=\"#/class/RopeConstraint/RopeConstraint.WinchForce\"><code>WinchForce</code></a></li>\n                    <li><a class=\"ref\" href=\"#/class/RopeConstraint/RopeConstraint.WinchSpeed\"><code>WinchSpeed</code></a></li>\n                </ul>\n            </td>\n        </tr>\n    </tbody>\n</table>\n\n<h2>Additional wake situations</h2>\n<p>In addition to situations outlined in <a href=\"#sleep-checking\">sleep‑checking</a> and <a href=\"#sleeping\">sleeping</a>, an assembly enters the <a href=\"#awake\">awake</a> state when:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>It collides with another assembly moving faster than 1 studs/s.</li>\n<li>\n<p>Any physics-related property of any <a class=\"ref\" href=\"#/class/BasePart\"><code>BasePart</code></a> within the assembly changes, including:</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><a class=\"ref\" href=\"#/class/BasePart/BasePart.Anchored\"><code>Anchored</code></a></p>\n</li>\n<li><a class=\"ref\" href=\"#/class/BasePart/BasePart.AssemblyLinearVelocity\"><code>AssemblyLinearVelocity</code></a>/<a class=\"ref\" href=\"#/class/BasePart/BasePart.AssemblyAngularVelocity\"><code>AssemblyAngularVelocity</code></a></li>\n<li><a class=\"ref\" href=\"#/class/BasePart/BasePart.CanCollide\"><code>CanCollide</code></a>/<a class=\"ref\" href=\"#/class/BasePart/BasePart.CanTouch\"><code>CanTouch</code></a></li>\n<li><a class=\"ref\" href=\"#/class/BasePart/BasePart.CustomPhysicalProperties\"><code>CustomPhysicalProperties</code></a></li>\n<li><a class=\"ref\" href=\"#/class/BasePart/BasePart.EnableFluidForces\"><code>EnableFluidForces</code></a></li>\n<li><a class=\"ref\" href=\"#/class/BasePart/BasePart.Massless\"><code>Massless</code></a></li>\n<li>\n<p><a class=\"ref\" href=\"#/class/BasePart/BasePart.RootPriority\"><code>RootPriority</code></a></p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>A non-zero impulse is applied to any <a class=\"ref\" href=\"#/class/BasePart\"><code>BasePart</code></a> within the assembly via <a class=\"ref\" href=\"#/class/BasePart/BasePart:ApplyImpulse\"><code>ApplyImpulse()</code></a>, <a class=\"ref\" href=\"#/class/BasePart/BasePart:ApplyImpulseAtPosition\"><code>ApplyImpulseAtPosition()</code></a>, or <a class=\"ref\" href=\"#/class/BasePart/BasePart:ApplyAngularImpulse\"><code>ApplyAngularImpulse()</code></a>.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Any physics-related property changes on the <a class=\"ref\" href=\"#/class/Workspace\"><code>Workspace</code></a> that would affect the assembly, including:</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><a class=\"ref\" href=\"#/class/Workspace/Workspace.Gravity\"><code>Gravity</code></a></p>\n</li>\n<li><a class=\"ref\" href=\"#/class/Workspace/Workspace.FluidForces\"><code>FluidForces</code></a></li>\n<li><a class=\"ref\" href=\"#/class/Workspace/Workspace.GlobalWind\"><code>GlobalWind</code></a></li>\n<li>\n<p><a class=\"ref\" href=\"#/class/Workspace/Workspace.AirDensity\"><code>AirDensity</code></a></p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>A new <a class=\"ref\" href=\"#/class/Constraint\"><code>Constraint</code></a> is created with an <a class=\"ref\" href=\"#/class/Attachment\"><code>Attachment</code></a> that is parented to a <a class=\"ref\" href=\"#/class/BasePart\"><code>BasePart</code></a> within the assembly.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Any property changes for a <a class=\"ref\" href=\"#/class/Constraint\"><code>Constraint</code></a> with an <a class=\"ref\" href=\"#/class/Attachment\"><code>Attachment</code></a> that is parented to a <a class=\"ref\" href=\"#/class/BasePart\"><code>BasePart</code></a> within the assembly.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>The <a class=\"ref\" href=\"#/class/Motor/Motor.CurrentAngle\"><code>CurrentAngle</code></a> property changes for a <a class=\"ref\" href=\"#/class/Motor\"><code>Motor</code></a> that is connected to a <a class=\"ref\" href=\"#/class/BasePart\"><code>BasePart</code></a> within the assembly.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>The assembly contains a <a class=\"ref\" href=\"#/class/VehicleSeat\"><code>VehicleSeat</code></a> with a seated player character.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>The assembly is within the <a class=\"ref\" href=\"#/class/Explosion/Explosion.BlastRadius\"><code>BlastRadius</code></a> of an <a class=\"ref\" href=\"#/class/Explosion\"><code>Explosion</code></a>.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Debug visualization</h2>\n<p>During playtesting, you can visualize assembly sleep states by toggling on <strong>Awake&nbsp;parts</strong> from the <a href=\"https://create.roblox.com/docs/studio/ui-overview#visualization-options\">Visualization&nbsp;Options</a> widget in the upper‑right corner of the 3D viewport.</p>\n<p><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"data:image/webp;base64,\" alt=\"A close up view of the 3D viewport with the Visualization Options button indicated in the upper-right corner.\" /></p>\n<p>Once enabled, simulated parts will be outlined by their current sleep state, with <a href=\"#awake\">awake</a> parts outlined in red, <a href=\"#sleep-checking\">sleep‑checking</a> parts outlined in orange, and <a href=\"#sleeping\">sleeping</a> parts un‑outlined.</p>\n<figure>\n  <video class=\"gmedia\" controls preload=\"none\" src=\"g/assets/physics/assemblies/Sleep-Demo.mp4\" data-alt=\"\"></video>\n  <figcaption>Simulated parts outlined by the color representing their current sleep state</figcaption>\n</figure>","kid":{"simple":"Roblox has to keep track of every moving thing in your game, and that takes work. The sleep system saves that work by letting objects that are sitting still 'fall asleep', so the engine skips them. When something bumps them or changes, they wake up again. Knowing this helps you understand why a very slow-moving part might suddenly stop, and how to keep it moving.","analogy":"It is like a teacher who only watches the students who are moving around. Kids sitting quietly are skipped, but the moment one of them gets nudged or stands up, the teacher pays attention again.","keyPoints":["Every assembly is always in one of three states: awake (simulated), sleeping (skipped), or sleep-checking (skipped, but checking if it should wake).","An assembly falls asleep when it is moving slower than about 0.33 studs per second and is not speeding up.","The acceleration check stops mistakes, like a ball thrown up falling asleep at the very top where it is almost still.","A still assembly connected to an awake neighbor goes into sleep-checking and wakes up if that neighbor starts moving fast enough.","Parts driven slowly by motors and other actuated joints (like a `HingeConstraint` set to `Motor`) get a stricter rule, so they can move slowly without falling asleep.","Things that wake an assembly include: being hit by something moving faster than 1 stud per second, changing physics properties like `Anchored` or `AssemblyLinearVelocity`, applying an impulse, changing `workspace.Gravity`, adding or changing a constraint on it, or an explosion nearby.","To see sleep states while playtesting, turn on Awake parts in the Visualization Options in the top-right of the viewport. Red outline means awake, orange means sleep-checking, no outline means sleeping."],"terms":{"assembly":"A group of parts joined together that physics moves as one solid object, called a rigid body.","rigid body":"An object that never bends or squishes. Physics only needs its position and speed to move it.","simulate":"Have the physics engine calculate how something moves, bit by bit, every moment.","threshold":"A cut-off number. Below 0.33 studs per second counts as 'not moving'; above it counts as moving.","linear velocity":"How fast something moves from place to place, in studs per second.","rotational velocity":"How fast a point on the edge of the object moves because the object is spinning.","acceleration":"How fast the speed is changing. A ball sitting on a slope that is about to roll has acceleration even if it is still for a moment.","worldstep":"One tiny step of the physics calculation. Roblox does many of these every second.","actuated joint":"A constraint that actively drives movement, like a motor or a winch, instead of just holding parts together.","impulse":"A quick, sudden push, like a kick, given with functions such as `ApplyImpulse()`.","bounding sphere":"An imaginary ball just big enough to hold every part of the assembly. Spin speed is measured at its edge, so big objects count as moving faster for the same spin."},"watchOut":["If a part stops moving when you expected it to keep sliding, it may have fallen asleep because it was too slow. Give it a bit more speed, or wake it with a property change or impulse.","Sleeping parts are not broken. They wake up automatically when something touches them or changes.","Big assemblies can spin slower without sleeping than small ones, because spin is measured at the edge of their bounding sphere."]}}